{"summary": "Full GAAIA discussion-draft comment package (work order FRC-POL-2026-062), drafted to board-approved positions in messaging_guide_v4.md and the briefing folder, with every external fact checked against the sponsors' section-by-section, law-firm and policy analyses, and primary sources. Six deliverables in /workspace/out/ plus a sourcing notes file.", "deliverables": ["/workspace/out/comment_letter_GAAIA.md", "/workspace/out/hill_one_pager.md", "/workspace/out/asks_by_section.md", "/workspace/out/social_posts.md", "/workspace/out/newsletter_blurb.md", "/workspace/out/staff_qa.md", "/workspace/out/_research_notes.md"], "notes_for_reviewers": "SPEC COMPLIANCE: (1) comment letter 1,880 words (1,500-2,200 band), signed Dr. Miriam Achterberg, Executive Director, addressed to Reps. Obernolte and Trahan via GAAIA@mail.house.gov, cites draft sections throughout; (2) one-pager 448 words (<=450), headline + 5 asks; (3) asks_by_section table with all four required columns, 14 provision rows; (4) five social posts, all 241-268 characters (<=280), labeled X/LinkedIn; (5) newsletter blurb exactly 150 words of prose; (6) staff_qa answers 113/117/111/115 words (<=120 each), keyed to the four questions in briefing/staff_questions.md.

FACT-CHECKING: The briefing's "Section numbers: TODO" flag is resolved. Section numbers were verified against the sponsors' section-by-section summaries (obernolte.house.gov, trahan.house.gov) plus ArentFox Schiff, DLA Piper, McDonald Hopkins, Roll Call, FedScoop, FPF and Lawfare. Every date, figure and quotation in the package is sourced in _research_notes.md, including: Sec. 101 frontier-model threshold (>10^26 operations - the same line as our moratorium ask), Sec. 102 CAISI $100M/yr FY2027-29, Sec. 111 15-day/24-hour incident reporting, Sec. 112 semi-annual developer-paid IVO audits and $1M/day penalties, the three-year sunset on Secs. 111-112, Sec. 121's broad "development" definition and its carve-outs, SB 53 in force 1 Jan 2026, NY RAISE effective 1 Jan 2027 with a 72-hour clock, the Senate's 99-1 preemption vote of 1 July 2025, the 16 Dec 2025 EO creating the DOJ AI Litigation Task Force, the 29 Sep 2026 White House Accord, the 9 Oct 2026 26-researcher pause-feasibility study, and Anthropic's 4 Jun 2026 statement. Polling figures are cited as FRC's own Aug 2026 survey. No member names appear anywhere (no consent flags exist in the briefing folder).

JUDGMENT CALLS FLAGGED TO THE POLICY DIRECTOR (auto-reply confirms he is not monitoring the queue this run): (a) treating Sec. 113 whistleblower protections, Sec. 311 open-source grants, Secs. 131-132 penalties and Sec. 401 testbeds as provisions we support - my read, not a stated board position; (b) including subordinate fallback asks in the section table under the primary replace-with-moratorium position. Both are easy to strip before the ED signs. Letterhead, date and contact block are bracketed placeholders for comms, per "drafts only - nothing is sent from this workspace.""}
